`@styles` provides compile-time inline CSS fragments for the `style` slots exposed by `@html`. It carries Core origin with MothSource backing. See @../../#package-origins-and-backing (Package origins and backing) for origin and backing rules.

The compiler reads `packages/styles/@mod.moth`, and the common builder surface registers the root under every builder, including custom SDK builders. A project cannot replace the package or remove it from the `.mtf` prelude.

### Exports

Every export is a compile-time `#String`. The value is one styled template fragment with a trailing semicolon:

[table:
    [th:
        [: Constant]
        [: CSS]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `center`]
        [: `text-align: center;`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `right`]
        [: `text-align: right;`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `left`]
        [: `text-align: left;`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `smaller`]
        [: `font-size: smaller;`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `medium`]
        [: `font-size: medium;`]
    ]

    [td:
        [: `larger`]
        [: `font-size: larger;`]
    ]
]

### Relationship to `@html` slots

Each fragment is written as an `$in style:` contribution. Template heads pass the constant by name, so the CSS lands in the `style` attribute exposed by the `@html` helper:

[codeblock, $code "text":
    [h1, center: A centred heading.]
]

A `.moth` file binds constants before it builds or inserts a template:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @styles center, larger
]

The fragments carry no runtime behaviour and need no runtime assets. Only compile-time constants enter the `.mtf` prelude. Functions, types and private constants require an explicit dependency clause in `.moth` files.

### Prelude contribution

`@styles` contributes all six constants to the fixed `.mtf` prelude. A public constant declared by the package enters that prelude even when another file in the package exports it. A re-export of another package's declaration does not. See @../html/#html-helpers (HTML helpers) and @../../../moth-templates/#template-scope (Template scope).

### Related concepts

- For the markup helpers that expose these slots see @../html/ (@html).
- For the package origin and backing model see @../../#package-origins-and-backing (Package origins and backing).
- For dependency-path rules see @../../#dependency-paths (Dependency paths).
